<h1>Oromo interpreter and translation services in the Twin Cities</h1>
<p class="sub">Apple Tree Interpreters provides Oromo interpreting and translation for medical, legal, education, and community settings across Minneapolis, St. Paul, and the surrounding area. In person, by phone, or by video, and available 24/7.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/interpreting/#request">Request an interpreter</a><a class="btn btn-green" href="/translation/#request">Request a translation</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="tel:+16124008903"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-phone"/></svg>(612) 400-8903</a></div>
</div></div></div>
<section id="about"><div class="wrap">
<div class="head"><h2>About Oromo (Afaan Oromoo) interpreting and translation</h2><p>Afaan Oromoo is one of the most widely spoken languages in Africa, and Minnesota is home to one of the largest Oromo communities in the United States.</p></div>
<ul class="perks two">
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-globe"/></svg></div><div><b>Written in the Latin alphabet</b><span>Oromo is written with a Latin-based alphabet called Qubee, so it looks familiar to English readers, but spelling and grammar are very different.</span></div></li>
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-globe"/></svg></div><div><b>Regional variety</b><span>Oromo has regional varieties. Tell us where the person is from when you request an interpreter so we can match as closely as possible.</span></div></li>
</ul></div></section>
<section id="services" class="request stack"><div class="wrap">
<div class="head"><h2>How we can help with Oromo</h2><p>Qualified, trained language professionals who show up prepared, with attention to accuracy and confidentiality.</p></div>
<ul class="perks two">
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg></div><div><b><a href="/interpreting/medical/">Medical settings</a></b><span>Oromo interpreting for clinics, hospitals, dental offices, and other healthcare visits.</span></div></li>
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-doc"/></svg></div><div><b><a href="/interpreting/legal/">Legal settings</a></b><span>Oromo interpreting for attorney meetings, depositions, and other legal situations.</span></div></li>
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg></div><div><b><a href="/interpreting/community/">Community and government</a></b><span>Oromo interpreting for government agencies and programs, schools, nonprofits, and community organizations.</span></div></li>
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-pin"/></svg></div><div><b>In-person interpreting</b><span>On-site interpreters across the Twin Cities.</span></div></li>
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-video"/></svg></div><div><b>Phone and video interpreting</b><span>Fast remote access for urgent needs, clinics, and remote offices.</span></div></li>
<li><div class="ib"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-doc"/></svg></div><div><b>Document translation</b><span>Written translation of forms, letters, and notices into and out of Oromo.</span></div></li>
</ul></div></section>
