<div class="head"><h2>Request a Oromo interpreter or translator</h2><p>Choose the service you need. Most requests are confirmed within 2 hours.</p></div>
<div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/interpreting/#request">Request an interpreter</a><a class="btn btn-green" href="/translation/#request">Request a translation</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="tel:+16124008903"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-phone"/></svg>(612) 400-8903</a></div>
</div></section>
<section id="faq" class="request stack"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><h2>Oromo frequently asked questions</h2></div><details><summary>Is Oromo written in the same alphabet as English?</summary><p>Oromo uses a Latin-based alphabet, but that does not make it easy to translate by sight. Documents should be handled by a qualified translator.</p></details><details><summary>Can I request a Oromo interpreter by phone or video?</summary><p>Yes. Phone and video interpreting is available for urgent needs and short conversations. Call (612) 400-8903 or use our request options.</p></details><details><summary>Do you translate documents into and out of Oromo?</summary><p>Yes. Request a quote on our translation page with the document type, languages, and deadline. Please do not send documents until we confirm a secure method.</p></details><details><summary>How quickly can I get a Oromo interpreter?</summary><p>Most requests are confirmed within 2 hours, and we are available 24/7, including weekends. Availability can vary by language and setting, so call us for urgent needs.</p></details></div></section>
